            <ArticleTitle>Ibuprofen-induced Henoch-Schönlein purpura nephritis: First reported case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>739-740</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0253-7613.194848</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ibuprofen is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug that is used widely in treating pain, fever, and inflammation. Its side effects are mainly due to acute renal impairment and gastric discomfort. We hereby report a rare case of Henoch-Schönlein purpura nephritis secondary to ibuprofen consumption which has not been reported in literature before.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
